gradients: [('The prompt may have gotten these examples wrong because it lacks clarity in distinguishing between objective factual statements and subjective interpretations or opinions. Additionally, the prompt does not specify how to handle statements that are context-dependent or that may require external knowledge to verify their accuracy. This can lead to confusion in evaluating the truthfulness of statements that involve political claims or nuanced contexts, resulting in incorrect classifications. Furthermore, the prompt might not adequately encourage the classifier to consider the reliability of the sources or the potential biases related to the job title and party affiliation mentioned, which are crucial for accurate evaluation.', '## Example 1\nText: "Statement: In Oregon, 12,808 people were arrested for marijuana-related crimes in 2012.\nJob title: Activist group\nState: Oregon\nParty: organization\nContext: a website statement"\nLabel: Yes\nPrediction: No\n\n## Example 2\nText: "Statement: On a cap-and-trade plan.\nJob title: \nState: \nParty: republican\nContext: a letter to the Minnesota delegation in Washington"\nLabel: Yes\nPrediction: No\n\n## Example 3\nText: "Statement: Voter fraud provided a portion of the margin of victory of Democrat John Lehman over Republican Sen. Van Wanggaard in a state Senate recall election.\nJob title: Wisconsin Assembly speaker\nState: Wisconsin\nParty: republican\nContext: a television interview"\nLabel: Yes\nPrediction: No\n\n## Example 4\nText: "Statement: In New York City, an entry level janitor gets paid twice as much as an entry level teacher.\nJob title: Co-host on CNN\'s "Crossfire"\nState: Georgia\nParty: republican\nContext: a Republican presidential debate in Des Moines, Iowa"\nLabel: Yes\nPrediction: No')]
